Hold the custom shade boxes above the off sentinel

The first custom shade and the first custom alpha carry the off state of
their group. A first element at or below 0.00001 means that the group is
off. The spin boxes accepted 0.00, so a user who typed that value in the
first box switched the group off. The rest of the row went with it.

The boxes also kept the two decimals of the Qt default. The style holds
three-decimal constants, so a box showed 0.055 as 0.06 and 0.782 as
0.78. A stored value below 0.005 showed as 0.00, and the next save then
wrote the sentinel over a group that was on.

The setup functions now give each box three decimals. They also give the
first box of each group a minimum of 0.001. The group check box stays
the one way to switch a group off, and the file format does not change.

The change sits on the branch work/dialog-state of the local tree, as commit 5 of 12.
A new merge request on system/qtcurve takes that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

diff --git a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
index 67e8cdb4..92e33b71 100644
--- a/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
+++ b/qt6/config/qtcurveconfig.cpp
@@ -2411,9 +2411,17 @@ void QtCurveConfig::setupShadesTab()
     connect(qtcSlot(customAlphas, toggled), qtcSlot(this, updateChanged));
 }
 
+// The number of decimals of a custom shade box and of a custom alpha box.
+static const int    constShadeDecimals = 3;
+// The smallest value of the first box of each group. The first custom shade
+// and the first custom alpha hold the off sentinel of their group. The
+// sentinel is a value at or below 0.00001.
+static const double constMinFirstShade = 0.001;
+
 void QtCurveConfig::setupShade(QDoubleSpinBox *w, int shade)
 {
-    w->setRange(0.0, 2.0);
+    w->setDecimals(constShadeDecimals);
+    w->setRange(0==shade ? constMinFirstShade : 0.0, 2.0);
     w->setSingleStep(0.05);
     connect(qtcSlot(w, valueChanged, (double)), qtcSlot(this, updateChanged));
     shadeVals[shade] = w;
@@ -2421,7 +2429,8 @@ void QtCurveConfig::setupShade(QDoubleSpinBox *w, int shade)
 
 void QtCurveConfig::setupAlpha(QDoubleSpinBox *w, int alpha)
 {
-    w->setRange(0.0, 1.0);
+    w->setDecimals(constShadeDecimals);
+    w->setRange(0==alpha ? constMinFirstShade : 0.0, 1.0);
     w->setSingleStep(0.05);
     connect(qtcSlot(w, valueChanged, (double)), qtcSlot(this, updateChanged));
     alphaVals[alpha] = w;
